# L §6.1 Identities are written: "each side names a kind, a thing (a keyed place at its keys included), ... with its
# keys written as literals"; Consolidation: "A binding over places of several members counts each place once"; rows
# stated same (here the two openings, one thing's facts) are read together and agree. a.sav[kid] and b.sav[kid] are one
# place; ana's deposit and ben's record of it are one movement (same a.dep = b.dep_seen), booked once. By L §5.10's bal
# (opening plus legs): 10.00 + 100.00 = 110.00 PLN, read by either name; one account; each member alone (a.q, b.q)
# also has 110.00 PLN. A key written as a literal after a member's item is that member's thing (a.sav[kid], as L §6.1's
# a.due[ola, 2025]).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "68706e69477e3e58a03c8045cca0809eba9f753f7565facf19ce427acf620205"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "54159463b5a74aaebc2daa3a80fbc1f9ec515d3158565f215238532203146b34"
  same a.persons = b.persons
  same a.kid = b.kid
  same a.sav[kid] = b.sav[kid]
  same a.dep = b.dep_seen

ask ka: bal(a.sav[kid], 2026-12-31)
ask kb: bal(b.sav[a.kid], 2026-12-31)
ask n: count(p in accounts on 2026-12-31)
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place sav[p in persons]: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input dep_amt: money PLN
input dep_day: date

move dep: transfers
  on dep_day
  leg cash from world to sav[kid] amount dep_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [kid] lives 2019-01-01..
  dep_amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  dep_day = 2026-03-01 "plan"
  opening[sav[kid]] = 10.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask q: bal(sav[kid], 2026-12-31)
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place sav[p in persons]: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place from_ana: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input dep_amt: money PLN
input dep_day: date

move dep_seen: transfers
  on dep_day
  leg cash from from_ana to sav[kid] amount dep_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [kid] lives 2019-01-01..
  dep_amt = 100.00 PLN "plan"
  dep_day = 2026-03-01 "plan"
  opening[sav[kid]] = 10.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask q: bal(sav[kid], 2026-12-31)
=== expect ka kb n a.q b.q
ka: 110.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-05
kb: 110.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-05
n: 1
  cut 2026-01-05
a.q: 110.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-05
b.q: 110.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-05
